Unix process control commands
a command issued in unix/linux start a new process, which invokes a 5 digit unique id is pid


INITIALIZING A PROCESS
 A process can be initialized in two ways, foreground and background
    Foreground
         Every process runs in foreground by default when it is started
         $ ls pwd
    Background
        Runs in the background allowing other processes to run in parallel
         $ pwd &
         ls || pwd &
         ls && pwd &

TRACKING A PROCESS 
ps - current running process
ps aux - all running process

